bar to  speak I want to thank leader Pelosi for  her incredible leadership her incredible  female leadership and the strength and  the power that she brings to this caucus  every single day to congressmen the  congresswoman DeLauro thank you thank  you thank you for your relentless  leadership on this issue for your  determination to make sure that this  never fell to the backburner and that  you have you will consistently remind  this caucus this Congress this country  that we have a long way to go and I'm so  grateful for that and yes thank you  to Michelle Williams thank you for those  beautiful words thank you for sharing  such a personal story for lending your  fame and your voice to helping uplift  other women we're so grateful and to my  sisters standing behind me my sisters  who were on the House floor to all of  the women of this country we deserve  better it is incredible that it is the  year 2019 and we are still talking about  issues related to women being  second-class citizens because my friends  indeed that's what this is about  when we look at whose health care is  most threatened when we look at whose  livelihoods are most threatened and when  we look at who shoulders the vast  majority of the burden in this country  it is the woman we expect women to raise  our kids to clean our homes to plan for  the future to be the center of the  family to go to work to earn a living  all things that we do with grace and and  we do with every inch of our being and  we provide dignity in all that we do to  deserve equal pay is a bare minimum a  bare minimum of what we should be  fighting for in this country and it is  shameful that today we are still  fighting that fight but there is so much  hope in this Congress in this body of  women in the leadership that women have  provided and in the way that women this  year have said enough and so together  this is but the first step that we will  be taking as we continue to fight for  stronger values that make America the  great country that she is a country that  is led by women thank you  and I want to introduce a fantastic  leader an incredible voice and my  co-chair for the Democratic Women's  Caucus my dear friend Deb Holland from  New Mexico thank you thank you all so  much for taking the time to be here this  afternoon the fact that we're standing  here for months in two days into the air  the amount of time it takes a woman to  earn what her male counterpart earned  last year tells us that there's still a  problem I'll tell you something else  it's worse for women of color  we'll be marking latina and Native  American equal pay day in June that's  six months into the year there are  people who will deny that this is an  issue we should be addressing but let me  tell you what it means to a family it  means the difference between several  months rent each year or some trips to  the grocery store each month can you  imagine what the impact is for a single  mom without any other income stream I  know what it's like because I have a  single mom when you get to the checkout  stand and have to figure out which items  that you have to put back because you  don't have enough in your account  back that women earn less money for the  same jobs as men it's about fairness and  we're taking action the Paycheck  Fairness Act is needed and I'm proud it  passed on the House floor last week if  we can get this done it will mean the  world for women and their children who  are working hard to make ends meet thank  you all so much and I hand it back to my  colleague and I am here to say thank you  all for being here today let's keep our  eyes on the Senate and Michelle Williams  thank you again for joining us thank you  [Applause]
 

